le negative numbers to ensure the minimum sum is found.\\n\\n4. **Edge Cases**:\\n   - Empty list: Raise `ValueError`.\\n   - Single-element list: Return the single element.\\n   - List with all negative numbers: Return the smallest negative number.\\n\\n5. **Complexity**:\\n   - Time: O(n), where n is the length of `nums`.\\n   - Space: O(1), as only a few variables are used.\\n\\n6. **Example Implementations**:\\n   ```python\\n   def minSubArraySum(nums: list) -> int:\\n       if not nums:\\n           raise ValueError(\\"Input list cannot be empty\\")\\n       if len(nums) == 1:\\n           return nums[0]\\n       \\n       min_sum = nums[0]\\n       current_sum = 0\\n       \\n       for num in nums:\\n           current_sum += num\\n           if current_sum < min_sum:\\n               min_sum = current_sum\\n           if current_sum < 0:\\n               current_sum = 0\\n       \\n       return min_sum\\n   ```\\n\\n7. **Testing**:\\n   - Test with an empty list.\\n   - Test with a single-element list.\\n   - Test with a list of positive numbers.\\n   - Test with a list of negative numbers.\\n   - Test with a mixed list of positive and negative numbers."}'}]
